Skills: default

Purpose:
  Define engineering rules and implementation patterns organized by
  technology and competency layers. Skills tell AI HOW to do work,
  not WHAT to do.

Domains:
  languages:
    path: ./languages
    purpose: Programming language skills by layer (L1-L5)

  frameworks:
    path: ./frameworks
    purpose: Framework skills by layer (L1-L4)

  databases:
    path: ./databases
    purpose: Database skills by layer (L1-L4)

  platforms:
    path: ./platforms
    purpose: Platform skills by layer (L1-L4)

  cross-cutting:
    path: ./cross-cutting
    purpose: Cross-cutting concerns (testing, security, architecture, observability)

Rules:
  [SK1] Skills MUST be referenced by ID only.
  [SK2] Skill content MUST be loaded on demand.
  [SK3] Skills MUST NOT contain project-specific knowledge.
  [SK4] Skills MUST define inputs, outputs, and validation.
  [SK5] Skills MUST be stage-specific.
  [SK6] Skills MUST be organized by technology and competency layer.

State: +
